> Since I've been struggling to get a character past Exp Lvl 10 I've been 
> reading some tips online.  There are some that suggest that you stay on 
> D-lvl 1 until you hit E-lvl 3 and then try to keep your E-lvl 1 above
> the D-lvl you're on.

It depends what class you're playing. For non-fighter roles until you hit
exp. level 7 or so or 50 hp go down one level for every 2 gained. That is
don't decend to level 2 until 3rd level, level 3 until 5th. Don *not* do
into the mines until you're at 50 hp and hopefully at or below ac 0. Do
the adjacent level to the mines before you think of going into it. Have a
chest/box waiting beside the mine entrance. At up staircase of every 5th
level and sokoban helps too. For fighters, the rules differ. The 50 hp
rule still applies, but getting to the mine entrance is quicker as you
gain hp quicker and your str is usually higher. Don't worry about using
metal armor if you're a spell caster at first. Anything that drops your AC
and allows you to fight/throw daggers better is needed early as possible.
Your first hunt should be a floating eye to kill and eat. Best to let your
pet get paralyzed by it by attacking it so you can kill it with
projectiles and eat it before your pet can get at it. 

