Monsters to eat, monsters dropping food. Chests/boxes are an early thing
to open with an *edged* weapon or key/lockpick (if you get one early). 

> So, what would you veteran players suggest?  Should I just suck it up
> and stick to a formula of not hitting the next D-lvl until I'm a E-lvl
> or two ahead of it, or will I find that a strategy like that will just
> leave me with a pile of starved corpses? 
> 
You don't want a pile, you want normal food and corpses when your a) not
satiated and b) your pet doesn't get to it first. leave the small stuff
(newts and geko's) for your pet. 

You mention exp. 10 at the top. Is the top level of sokoban a problem? try
converting an altar (*not* minetown) before you enter it and then go back
and sac until you get a clover just before you would open the last room.
Then go back and sit at the doorway and let them come to you.


